# Places in a container image where tooling packages live: software that only
# builds or installs the image's contents and is never loaded by the running
# service. Read by lib/security/analyse.py. A vulnerability whose packages were
# all found in such places is never urgent (docs/adr/0010).
#
# One Python regular expression per line, matched against the file path Syft
# found the package at. No spaces.

# Package managers installed globally (npm ships with Node.js).
/(usr|usr/local|opt/[^/]+)/lib/node_modules/(npm|pnpm|yarn|corepack)/
/usr/local/share/\.?(npm|yarn|corepack)/
# pnpm's content-addressed store and the pnpm versions it downloads itself.
/\.local/share/pnpm/
/\.pnpm-store/
/\.cache/(pnpm|yarn|node/corepack)/
# Executables that npm packages ship (git hooks, bundlers, linters), e.g. lefthook.
/node_modules/\.pnpm/[^/]+/node_modules/(@[^/]+/)?[^/]+/bin/
/node_modules/(@[^/]+/)?[^/]+/bin/[^/]+$
